// data/ob/italian.ron — Italian Order of Battle (§4.44b). Reference data (D12): the full
// campaign roster; scenarios select + place formations from it.
//
// CHART-VERIFIED (D14 retired for the loaded formations, 2026-08-30): the loaded formations were
// checked against the §4.44b Italian OA sheets (transcribed from the rulebook PDF to
// docs/source-materials/it-ob-4.44b.transcribed.md). 64 Catanzaro (PDF p153), 132 Ariete (p147),
// and 185 Folgore (p154) all match exactly — ids, weapon systems, morale, and arrivals confirmed;
// no corrections required. The line-infantry "u" codes and the artillery/AT weapon strings are
// thus verified, not provisional. 62 Marmarica and 63 Cirene have NO §4.44b OA sheet (they appear
// only in the Libyan Tank Command notes) — confirming the D13 "abstracted semi-motorized template"
// decision. The remaining ~30 Italian formations have since been promoted (see the FULL ROSTER
// PROMOTED note below); all 38 §4.44b formations are now loaded.
//
// Ariete note: the two attached Light Tank battalions I(L)/II(L) have a BLANK id/TOE on the sheet
// (attached, not assigned); their "k" + CV 33 here is a reasonable inference, not chart-given.
//
// FULL ROSTER PROMOTED (2026-08-30) from the chart-verified transcription (all ids copied verbatim;
// every weapon name maps to an exact §4.48 key in data/reference/weapons/italian.ron). Decisions on
// non-obvious rows:
//   * Blank-id ATTACHED units that appear (with ids) on another sheet are OMITTED from their host
//     division to avoid duplicate/id-less counters: the CCNN legions/battalions attached to Pavia,
//     Bologna, Savona, Brescia (they live on the "Unassigned Blackshirt Units" sheet with ids);
//     I(M) attached to 1st CCNN, II(M) to Maletti, IX(L) to 2nd Libyan (all on the Libyan Tank
//     Command sheet with ids "l"/"k").
//   * "Unassigned Armored Units" prints a BLANK id for every row; since this sheet is that pool's
//     home roster (not an attachment listing), the units are INCLUDED with ids inferred
//     unambiguously from tank type + count (CV 33 light bns -> "k"; 7x M-series -> "l"), matching
//     the preserved Ariete I(L)/II(L)=k precedent. Inferred, not chart-given.
//   * Blank-id header/parent rows with no counter are dropped and their children reparented to the
//     Div HQ or left independent (parent ""): Littorio "3rd Articelere Regt"; the Tobruk/Bardia
//     "...Artiglieri" headers; the two "Artillery Ragruppamento" headers on the Unassigned Gun
//     sheet. The blank-id "San Giorgio" (a scuttled cruiser) is omitted.
//   * RECAM HQ's TOE reads a faint, un-keyable "1x vv" token -> modeled Organic(Normal) on id "a".
//   * Coastal-defense "'I' Light/Heavy AA" tokens map to the standard "Light AA (20mm M/35 Breda)"
//     / "Heavy AA (75/46 Mod. 34)" keys (no separate 'I' key exists).
//   * The two prose-only sections ("Italian Battle Groups", "Italian Blackshirt (CCNN) Units" intro)
//     are modeled as dynamic single-HQ formations; their HQ id "b" is inferred (prose has no id).
